BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Gift in Motion — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261029T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261029T170000
DTSTAMP:20261030T055419Z
UID:13bc291de831abaef79114e2e1be@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A multidisciplinary showcase from the artists and scholars of 
 the full-time faculty and staff at the Corcoran School of the Arts & Desig
 n. A Gift In Motion loosely draws from Robin Wall Kimmerer’s book The Se
 rviceberry which uplifts Indigenous frameworks of the natural world to adv
 ance the possibilities in collectivity\, reciprocity\, and the mindset of 
 abundance. These are anti-capitalist models and theories that provide insi
 ght into the systems of power we negotiate\, but also offer a lens on how 
 we individually move through our daily lives—together—through historic
 ally fraught landscapes. A keen reminder that working with\, for\, and bec
 ause of each other remains the most human motivation\, eve\nCategory: Arts
  & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/a-gift-in-mot
 ion
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/a-gift-in-motion
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Age-Friendly Ecosystem Summit Day 4 - More Than Shelter: Housing\,
  Loneliness\, and Social Connection — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261029T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261029T150000
DTSTAMP:20261030T055419Z
UID:a6438a4e5be395a1b23fe81a3c61@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Community Service\,Washington\, DC\,United Stat
 es
DESCRIPTION:Loneliness is a public health epidemic\, and housing is a powe
 rful\, often overlooked lever for addressing it\, shaping who we connect w
 ith and whether we feel embedded in community. This session explores how d
 ifferent housing models can rebuild social connection\, while confronting 
 the mental health toll of isolation and the barriers facing unhoused older
  adults. Speakers Paula Carder - Director\, Institute on Aging\, Portland 
 State University Samar Jha - Government Affairs Director\, AARP Sheila Jon
 es - Chief for Adult Protective Services\, Family Services Administration
 \, DC DHS Nancy Kelly - Charter member\, Village Hearth Cohousing Laurie T
 heeke - Professor\, George Washington University School of\nCategory: Comm
 unity Service\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/age-friend
 ly-ecosystem-summit-day-4-more-than-shelter-housing-loneliness-and-social-
 connection
LOCATION:George Washington University\, Washington\, DC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/age-friendly-ecosystem-summit-day-4-mor
 e-than-shelter-housing-loneliness-and-social-connection
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
