BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Diego Gerard Morrison: Writers on Writing — Providence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261029T173000
DTSTAMP:20261030T055419Z
UID:ecd509fad8ba26e0cd8af7def2a8@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\, Open to the Public\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Diego Gerard Morrison will take part in the Literary Arts seri
 es\, Writers on Writing. Diego Gerard Morrison (Mexico City\, 1984) is a w
 riter\, editor and translator whose recent work explores themes of Magical
  Realism and appropriation in the context of the Mexican drug war. His fir
 st book\, The Wait (John of the Thing\, 2021)\, is an appropriation of Sam
 uel Beckett’s Waiting for Godot in a setting of Mexican cartel violence 
 and its resulting crisis of forced disappearances. His debut novel\, Myth 
 of Pterygium (Autumn House Press\, 2022) was the winner of the Rising Priz
 e in Fiction. He is the author of the novel Pages of Mourning (Two Dollar 
 Radio\, 2024)\, and his book of stories Upflow (Split Lip\,\nCategory:  Op
 en to the Public\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/live/events/3
 35513-diego-gerard-morrison-writers-on-writing
LOCATION:70 Brown St.\, Providence\, 70 Brown St.\, Providence
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/live/events/335513-diego-gerard-morrison-writ
 ers-on-writing
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
