DESCRIPTION:Directed by Jodi I. Kanter Music by Douglas Boyce Feeling sad 
 has never been this sexy. Sarah Ruhl’s The Melancholy Play turns depress
 ion into an aphrodisiac and sadness into an art form. It’s a contemporar
 y farce about a woman so beautifully blue\, everyone is falling in love wi
 th her. Warning: Side effects may include sudden tree-nut transformations 
