 ates
DESCRIPTION:International broadcasting has been a key component of America
 's public diplomacy activities since World War II. Join us for our Novembe
 r First Monday Forum at which we will hear from the President and CEO of R
 adio Free Asia. The program will take place at noon on November 2 at GWU's
  Lindner Family Commons at the Elliott School (1957 E Street\, NW\, Room 6
 02\, Washington\, D.C. 20052). For those who RSVP and arrive before 11:40 
 a.m.\, a light lunch will be provided. The event is co-sponsored the GWU E
 lliott School of International Affairs\, the GW Institute for Public Diplo
 macy & Global Communication\, and the USC Annenberg Center on Communicatio
